    "source": "trade practice: equipment with a motor, heater, compressor or controls takes a branch circuit (NEC 422 appliances, 424 space heating, 430 motors, 440 A/C and refrigeration); manifolds, hoods and louvers without fans, gravity relief, tanks, valves, drains and dampers with no actuator (a fire damper closes on its fusible link) take none. An element with an electrical rating (volts, amps, MCA, horsepower, kW, VA) takes power whatever its name."
  },
